.TH "MIRU\-DAEMON" "1" "2026\-11\-12" "Miru" "miru\-daemon Manual"
.PP
.SH NAME
.PP
miru\-daemon \- Wayland\-native screen magnifier and cursor spotlight daemon
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
\fBmiru\-daemon\fR [options]
.PP
.SH DESCRIPTION
.PP
\fBmiru\-daemon\fR is a long\-running Wayland client.\& It connects to the compositor,
listens on a Unix socket, and stays idle until \fBmiructl\fR(1) sends a command.\&
.PP
On \fBtoggle\fR, it captures one frame via \fBwlr\-screencopy\fR, shows it in a
fullscreen \fBwlr\-layer\-shell\fR overlay, and lets you zoom, pan, highlight the
cursor, draw simple annotations, and open an on\-screen help panel.\& A second
\fBtoggle\fR (or \fBEsc\fR when help is closed) tears the overlay down.\& The underlying
desktop is not continuously re\-captured while the overlay is visible.\&
.PP
Control is only through \fBmiructl\fR(1) (\fBtoggle\fR / \fBquit\fR).\& Global hotkeys must
be bound in the compositor to run \fBmiructl toggle\fR.\&
.PP
.SH OPTIONS
.PP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
.RS 4
Print usage and exit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
.RS 4
Print version, then exit.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB\-\-gen\-config\fR, \fB\-\-interactive\fR
.RS 4
walk through options and write \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/miru/config.\&toml\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH COMMANDS (via miructl)
.PP
See \fBmiructl\fR(1).\& Typical usage:
.PP
.RS 4
miructl toggle
.PP
miructl quit
.PP
.RE
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.PP
\fBMIRU_DEBUG\fR
.RS 4
If set to a non\-zero value (e.\&g.\& \fB1\fR), print verbose diagnostics (input,
zoom, texture upload, annotate/help toggles, and similar).\& Unset or \fB0\fR
for normal logging.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBWAYLAND_DISPLAY\fR, \fBXDG_RUNTIME_DIR\fR
.RS 4
Standard Wayland / runtime directory variables.\& The control socket is
\fB$XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/miru.\&sock\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBXDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR
.RS 4
If set, config is read from \fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/miru/config.\&toml\fR;
otherwise \fB$HOME/.\&config/miru/config.\&toml\fR.\&
.PP
.RE
.SH CONFIGURATION
.PP
Config path:
.PP
.RS 4
$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/miru/config.\&toml
# or
$HOME/.\&config/miru/config.\&toml
.PP
.RE
The directory and a default file are created on first launch.\& The file is
watched; most options hot\-reload without restarting the daemon.\&
.PP
Default:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
[zoom]
factor = 2\&.0
increment = 0\&.25
max_factor = 10\&.0
smooth = false
upscale = "bicubic"

[spotlight]
radius = 250
dim = 0\&.65
softness = 20
animation_speed = 14\&.0
radius_step = 20\&.0
esc_quit = true

[general]
show_cursor = true
status_badge = false

[annotate]
default = "rect"
thickness = 4\&.0
color = "ff3333"
text_color = "ffd933"
text_size = 1\&.0

[loupe]
shape = "rect"

[export]
format = "png"

[filter]
default = "none"

[pip]
enabled = false
corner = "bottom\-right"
size = 0\&.2
margin = 16

[keybinds]
quit = "Esc"
help = "SHIFT+H, SHIFT+Slash"
export = "SHIFT+E"
refresh = "SHIFT+R"
toggle_cursor = "SHIFT+C"
toggle_highlight = "Tab"
annotate = "SHIFT+A"
toggle_pip = "SHIFT+P"
status_badge = "B"
cycle_filter = "F"
zoom_in = "Equal, SHIFT+Equal, KPPlus"
zoom_out = "Minus, SHIFT+Minus, KPMinus"
radius_up = "CTRL+Equal, CTRL+SHIFT+Equal, CTRL+KPPlus"
radius_down = "CTRL+Minus, CTRL+SHIFT+Minus, CTRL+KPMinus"
pan_left = "Left, A"
pan_right = "Right, D"
pan_up = "Up, W"
pan_down = "Down, S"
tool_arrow = "W"
tool_ellipse = "O"
tool_line = "L"
tool_rect = "R"
tool_text = "T"
tool_freehand = "P"
clear = "C"
undo = "CTRL+Z"
redo = "CTRL+Y, CTRL+SHIFT+Z"
.fi
.RE
.PP
\fB[zoom]\fR
.RS 4
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fBfactor\fR — initial zoom on each toggle\-on (min 1.\&0).\&  
.IP \(bu 4
\fBincrement\fR — zoom step for keys/scroll.\&  
.IP \(bu 4
\fBmax_factor\fR — maximum zoom.\&  
.IP \(bu 4
\fBsmooth\fR — interpolate zoom/pan when true.\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBupscale\fR \- Choose between \fBlinear\fR/\fBnormal\fR/\fBbicubic\fR for upscaling
.PD
.PP
.RE
\fB[spotlight]\fR (Cursor Highlight while magnifier is active, toggled with Tab)
.RS 4
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fBradius\fR, \fBdim\fR, \fBsoftness\fR — circle size, outside darkness, edge feather.\&  
.IP \(bu 4
\fBanimation_speed\fR — ease in/out speed for Tab.\&  
.IP \(bu 4
\fBradius_step\fR — step for Shift+Plus/Minus and Ctrl+scroll.\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBesc_quit\fR \- uses \fBESC\fR for quitting standalone spotlight mode.\&
.PD
.PP
.RE
\fB[general]\fR
.RS 4
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fBshow_cursor\fR — hide the hardware cursor while the overlay is active when
.RS 4
.PD
.RE
.RE
false (compositor\-dependent).\&
.RS 4
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fBstatus_badge\fR \- Choose to display the status badge (\fBtrue/false\fR)
.PD
.PP
.RE
\fB[annotate]\fR
.RS 4
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fBdefault\fR \- Default shape when entering annotation mode.\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBthickness\fR \- Thickness of the stroke (1\-8).\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBcolor\fR \- Hex RGB for annotation.\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBtext_size\fR \- Size of annotation text (0.\&25 \- 8.\&0).\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBtext_color\fR \- Hex RGB for annotation text.\&
.PD
.PP
.RE
\fB[loupe]\fR
.RS 4
\fBshape\fR \- Default shape when entering loupe mode
.PP
.RE
\fB[export]\fR
.RS 4
\fBformat\fR \- File format of exported image
.PP
.RE
\fB[filter]\fR
.RS 4
\fBdefault\fR \- The default image filter to apply when the overlay is active.\&
.PP
.RE
\fB[pip]\fR
.RS 4
.PD 0
.IP \(bu 4
\fBenabled\fR \- Shows the PIP minimap when the overlay opens (\fBtrue/false\fR).\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBcorner\fR \- \fBtop\-left, top\-right, bottom\-left, bottom\-right\fR.\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBsize\fR \- Width of the minimap as a fraction of the screen Width (0.\&05 \- 0.\&5).\&
.IP \(bu 4
\fBmargin\fR \- Distance from the screen edge in pixels.\&
.PD
.PP
.RE
\fB[keybinds]\fR
.RS 4
Rebinds the keys used while the overlay is active, e.\&g.\&
\fBhelp\fR = \fB"SHIFT+T"\fR or \fBexport = "E, CTRL+S"\fR.\& A value is comma\-separated.\&
You can use upto 4 bindings for each action; each is an optional
\fBSHIFT+\fR/\fBCTRL+\fR prefix followed by a key name (\fBA\fR, \fBEsc\fR, \fBTab\fR,
\fBEqual\fR.\&.\&.\&).\& Use \fB"none"\fR to unbind an action.\& These keys are unrelated to the
compositor\-level keybinds used to toggle the overlay.\&
.PP
.RE
Full detail:
https://codeberg.\&org/Vaishnav\-Sabari\-Girish/miru#configuration
.PP
.SH CONTROLS (while overlay is active)
.PP
The keys below are the defaults and can be changed in the \fB[keybinds]\fR section
of the config file.\&
.PP
\fBMouse move\fR
.RS 4
Pan.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBScroll\fR or \fB+\fR / \fB\-\fR
.RS 4
Zoom.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBWASD\fR / \fBarrow keys\fR
.RS 4
Pan (key repeat supported).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBTab\fR
.RS 4
Toggle Cursor Highlight.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShift+Plus\fR / \fBShift+Minus\fR or \fBCtrl+scroll\fR
.RS 4
Adjust highlight radius.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShift+A\fR
.RS 4
Toggle annotate mode (pan frozen; orange frame).\&  
\fBW\fR — arrow tool; \fBR\fR — rectangle; drag LMB — place; \fBCTRL+Z/Y\fR \- Undo/Redo; \fBP\fR \- freehand; \fBC\fR — clear.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBB\fR
.RS 4
Toggle Status Badge (Displays the zoom factor and the annotation tool chosen).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShift+P\fR
.RS 4
Toggle the PIP minimap; a small unzoomed copy of the captured screen with the
visible area outlined and the pointer marked.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBF\fR
.RS 4
Shift between different image filters (Normal, Grayscale, Inverted/Negative,
High Contrast).\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShift+H\fR or \fB?\&\fR
.RS 4
Toggle help panel.\& \fBEsc\fR closes help first if open.\&
.PP
.RE
\fBShift+E\fR
.RS 4
Export current view to a \fB.\&bmp\fR file.\& The file is stored at
\fB$HOME/Pictures/miru/\fR
.PP
.RE
\fBEsc\fR or compositor toggle keybind (\fBmiructl toggle\fR)
.RS 4
Exit magnifier (after closing help if needed).\&
.PP
.RE
.SH SYSTEMD
.PP
Example user unit \fB\(ti/.\&config/systemd/user/miru.\&service\fR:
.PP
.nf
.RS 4
[Unit]
Description=Miru Zooming Daemon
PartOf=graphical\-session\&.target
After=graphical\-session\&.target
ConditionEnvironment=WAYLAND_DISPLAY
ConditionPathExists=%h/\&.local/bin/miru\-daemon

[Service]
ExecStart=%h/\&.local/bin/miru\-daemon
Restart=on\-failure
RestartSec=1

[Install]
WantedBy=graphical\-session\&.target
.fi
.RE
.PP
.RS 4
systemctl \-\-user enable \-\-now miru.\&service
.PP
.RE
Adjust paths if binaries are installed elsewhere.\&
.PP
.SH KEYBINDS (compositor)
.PP
Bind a key to \fBmiructl toggle\fR in your compositor (Niri, Hyprland, Sway,
Mango, etc.\&).\& The daemon must already be running.\&
.PP
See:
https://codeberg.\&org/Vaishnav\-Sabari\-Girish/miru#setting\-up\-a\-keybind
.PP
.SH NOTES
.PP
Wayland does not expose a global pointer position while the overlay is
inactive.\& The zoom view prefers the last pointer position from a previous
session in the same daemon process when available.\&
.PP
Requires \fBwlr\-layer\-shell\-unstable\-v1\fR and \fBwlr\-screencopy\-unstable\-v1\fR.\&
GNOME (Mutter) and KDE Plasma (KWin) are not supported.\&
.PP
.SH SEE ALSO
.PP
\fBmiructl\fR(1)
.PP
